{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A vow.</b> One who says, 'Upon me is a קוֹנָם that I shall not eat,' or 'that I shall not do such-and-such a thing' — could it be even if he swore to eat נְבֵלוֹת, that I call upon him 'everything that proceeds from his mouth he shall fulfill'? Scripture says, <b>to forbid — a binding prohibition</b> — to forbid what is permitted, and not to permit what is forbidden (Sifrei)." "<b>He shall not profane his word.</b> As in לֹא יְחַלֵּל דְּבָרוֹ — he shall not make his word חֻלִּין (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:15.777666945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}